\section{Finite/kernel residuals and released locators}

The following machine delegations are finite rather than conceptual.  Each is
downstream of a human implication stated above.
\begin{description}[style=nextline,leftmargin=0pt,labelindent=0pt]
\item[\textnormal{Nondominant rational chase.}]
\texttt{theoremB\_chase\_left}, \texttt{theoremB\_chase\_right},
\texttt{theoremB\_hAR}, and \texttt{theoremB\_hRle} verify that the displayed
covering/dispersion dichotomy yields the explicit $X/\log^3X$ floor.

\item[\textnormal{Cold thresholds and rounding.}]
\texttt{cold\_master} and \texttt{cold\_no\_exceptions\_core} verify that a
fixed small forcing constant gives bounded and then empty exception sets.

\item[\textnormal{Level-set charge arithmetic.}]
\texttt{hrhs\_charge\_bound} and \texttt{hrhs\_final} perform the finite
integer-window and exponential rearrangements for the four-layer injective
code, yielding \eqref{eq:level-set}.

\item[\textnormal{Sector-I eventual domination.}]
\texttt{sectorI\_absorption'} verifies the final threshold at which the forcing
floor absorbs $e^{AJ}$ and $\sctrl^{-1}$.

\item[\textnormal{Inverse-square comparison.}]
\texttt{r2\_extra\_inv\_sq\_le} and the final \texttt{hsumE} assembly verify
that the noncontrol square load yields
\eqref{eq:inverse-square-constant}.

\item[\textnormal{Main-arc numeric fields.}]
\texttt{r2\_numericFields} and \texttt{r2\_close\_numericFields} verify the
Taylor disk, cubic remainder, and Gaussian window at the final scale.

\item[\textnormal{Terminal maximum.}]
\texttt{exists\_arcConstruction\_final} verifies that every threshold listed
in Step~4 is met by one $k_0$, with all constants already fixed.

\item[\textnormal{Finite tuple casts.}]
\texttt{Erdos306.erdos\_306} verifies the finite-index casts, increasing
enumeration, exclusion of the dummy anchor, and equality with the set sum.
\end{description}

